# Dictionary for `netplay_message`.
#
# Tag-byte-discriminated framing: byte 0 selects the variant and everything after it is that
# variant's body. Five tags out of 256 means a purely random first byte reaches a real decoder
# about 2% of the time; these tokens fix that.

# Tags: Sync, Input, InputAck, Checksum, Quality.
"\x00"
"\x01"
"\x02"
"\x03"
"\x04"

# `SYNC_MAGIC` (0x5253_4E50, "RSNP") little-endian, plus `PROTOCOL_VERSION` — the two fields a
# handshake has to satisfy before a session will accept anything else.
"PNSR"
"\x01\x00"

# Frame numbers on the wrap boundary. A rollback session indexes buffers by frame, so `u32::MAX`
# arriving from a remote peer is the interesting case.
"\xff\xff\xff\xff"
"\x00\x00\x00\x00"
"\xff\xff\xff\x7f"
